    "title": "pandas.Series.count — pandas 2.2.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.count#\n\n- Series.count()[source]#\n- Return number of non-NA/null observations in the Series. \n  - Returns:\n    - int\n    - Number of non-null values in the Series.\n See also \n  - `DataFrame.count`\n  - Count non-NA cells for each column or row.\n Examples >>> s = pd.Series([0.0, 1.0, np.nan]) >>> s.count() 2",
